      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "Plan grouped Claw agent updates",
        "body": "## Summary\r\n\r\n- add `openclaw.clawUpdatePlan.v1` for read-only, agent-centric reconciliation of a grouped Claw manifest\r\n- add `openclaw claws update <claw-or-agent> [--from <source>] --dry-run [--json]` behind `OPENCLAW_EXPERIMENTAL_CLAWS=1`\r\n- resolve the normal target from persisted add provenance; keep `--from` as an explicit override and recovery path\r\n- compare effective agent capabilities, workspace files, exact package refs, MCP declarations, and agent-pinned cron declarations\r\n- bind the complete preview to `planIntegrity` for the consented apply slice\r\n- perform no mutation: planning opens existing state read-only, does not create or migrate databases, and closes every owned handle\r\n\r\n## Planning contract\r\n\r\n- direct agent ids and unambiguous installed package names resolve to one root install record\r\n- older supported databases without Claws tables return structured `claw_not_found`\r\n- missing workspaces and owned artifacts are planned for restoration; unsafe roots, operator drift, ambiguous package identity, and incomplete ownership remain blocked\r\n- blocked actions produce a nonzero CLI result even when no separate diagnostic blocker exists\r\n- independently owned packages and MCP declarations cannot be restored or changed by a Claw\r\n- managed, Claw-introduced resources may be removed only when inspection proves they are unchanged and otherwise unused; referenced or independently owned resources are released\r\n- source MCP config is compared before placeholder resolution so credentials and local substitutions do not create false drift\r\n\r\n## Capability and consent contract\r\n\r\n- capability changes use secret-safe summaries plus SHA-256 digests of those summaries; raw MCP configuration and cron payloads never enter the plan model or secret-derived fingerprints\r\n- effective sandbox and heartbeat values come from OpenClaw's production resolvers, including inherited and implicit defaults\r\n- widening workspace access, sandbox sharing, tool access, plugin code, MCP surfaces, or scheduled automation requires distinct escalation consent\r\n- reductions and blocked removals do not request escalation consent\r\n\r\n## Real behavior proof\r\n\r\nCurrent head: `82bcde001d69249e9b880301ae6974d6e5296196`. The runtime transcript below was captured on earlier reviewed head `ee3b8d18037555a489652da707aa737eb3da4f0e`; exact-head tests cover the subsequent consent classification, ownership-release, and redacted-digest hardening.\r\n\r\nAn isolated v1 Claw was persisted through the production add-plan lifecycle, then the real CLI previewed v2 with a remote OAuth MCP URL containing `URL_SECRET_123`, a secret-like tool filter, and cron message `CRON_SECRET_ABC`.\r\n\r\nHuman preview:\r\n\r\n```text\r\nClaw update plan: @proof/safe-preview 1.0.0 -> 2.0.0\r\nAgent: safe-preview\r\nUpdate actions: 4\r\nCapability changes: 5; escalations requiring distinct consent: 3\r\n  - agent.sandbox.mode: off -> all (change)\r\n  - agent.sandbox.scope: agent -> session (change)\r\n  ! agent.sandbox.workspaceAccess: none -> ro (change)\r\n  ! cronJobs.private-report: unset -> schedule cron; session isolated; payload withheld (add)\r\n  ! mcpServers.private-search: unset -> remote server; auth configured; tool filter configured (add)\r\n```\r\n\r\nJSON emitted only paths, classifications, summaries, and digests. It contained none of `secret.example.test`, `URL_SECRET_123`, `PRIVATE_TOOL_SECRET_456`, or `CRON_SECRET_ABC`.\r\n\r\n## Verification\r\n\r\n- focused capability, update-planner, and CLI coverage: 55 tests passed\r\n- real Claw lifecycle E2E: 8 tests passed\r\n- broader Claw unit coverage: 95 tests passed during the restack\r\n- Oxfmt, focused Oxlint, max-lines ratchet, repository guardrails, import-cycle checks, and `git diff --check` passed\r\n- GitHub production and test type checks passed on the prior pushed tree; exact-head CI is running\r\n- exact-bundle GPT-5.5 autoreview of `82bcde001d6`: no actionable findings (`patch is correct`, confidence 0.84)\r\n\r\n## Stack\r\n\r\n- RFC: https://github.com/openclaw/rfcs/pull/27\r\n- Depends on: #102427 read-only diagnostics\r\n- This PR: authoritative read-only update planning and consent boundary\r\n- Next: #102982 executes only a freshly rebuilt, unblocked, consent-matched plan\r\n\r\n",
